cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use strhide in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "strhide: format-preserving lossless data hiding and content-adaptive steganography"
abstract: >-
  strhide is a Rust library, CLI, and desktop application for hiding data inside
  carrier files. Its structure domain injects an encrypted envelope into
  format-legal gaps (PNG chunks, JPEG APPn segments, ISO-BMFF boxes, RIFF chunks,
  ZIP central-directory slack, PDF incremental revisions, PE overlay/slack/instruction
  slots) and restores the pre-write host bit-exactly. Its content domain embeds
  payloads into pixels, DCT coefficients, HEVC CABAC bypass sign bits, and PCM/FLAC
  residuals using adaptive distortion cost models (HILL, S-UNIWARD, MiPOD, UERD,
  J-UNIWARD, J-MiPOD). Both domains use PBKDF2/HKDF key derivation and AEAD
  (AES-256-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305), and the wire formats are specified publicly for
  third-party implementations.
type: software
authors:
